    "abstract": "Araya et al., (2026). Copernicus Seasonal Forecast Tools Package: Bridging Seasonal Climate Predictions and Impact Models for Operational Risk Assessment. Journal of Open Source Software, 11(119), 8827, https://doi.org/10.21105/joss.08827",
    "field": "Climate risk assessment",
    "problem": "A lack of operational, reproducible tools creates a critical gap in connecting seasonal climate forecasts with impact models, as current workflows are fragmented and manual, hindering timely, quantitative risk assessments.",
    "method": "The proposed Copernicus Seasonal Forecast Tools Package provides an automated workflow to retrieve and process seasonal climate predictions from the Copernicus Climate Data Store and integrate them into the CLIMADA risk modeling pipeline for operational, impact-based risk assessment.",
    "task": "The task is to create a software package that automates the integration of seasonal climate predictions with impact models, bridging the gap between raw forecasts and actionable operational risk assessments.",
